<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's SFE wheat futures higher, more active.</title>
<headline>Australia's SFE wheat futures higher, more active.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traded Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) wheat futures moved higher on Wednesday with the January contract jumping A$5.50 to A$182.50 a tonne on a volume of 21 lots while the March contract contract rose A$5.50 to A$184 on a volume of just seven lots.</p>
<p>Settlement prices for the untraded contracts were higher.</p>
